--
-- CodeGen used to emit the join that fetches a related entity's name field (the `<FK>` display
-- column, e.g. `Agent` for `AgentID`) as INNER JOIN whenever the foreign-key column was NOT NULL,
-- and the same for the embedded-record geo join (`__mj_Latitude_<FK>`). Those joins exist only to
-- add a display value, but an INNER join decides whether the row survives: an unmatched or
-- mis-mapped related row removed the row from the view, silently. CodeGen now emits LEFT OUTER for
-- both, so a missing label is NULL and the row stays. IS-A parent joins are unchanged (INNER).
